From e866e6db88fcc10e9511e4d16584e6aabbc78ae4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mate Soos <soos.mate@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 23:22:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix an equivalence found on a lower dl overwriting an
 existing one

Bug: process_lineral() registers every active two-variable lineral as an
equivalence of its leading variable, asserting that the variable does not
have one already. That fails when the lineral is propagated late, on a lower
decision level than the current one: its reduction on that level ignores
the equivalences of higher levels, so the leading variable may already have
one. Debug builds abort with

  solver.hpp:908: process_lineral: Assertion `!equiv_lits[lt].is_active()' failed.

e.g. while processing x20+x481+1 on dl 15 (current dl 16) when x20 = x513
was recorded on dl 16. Release builds overwrite equiv_lits[20], which
leaves equiv_lits[513].prev_ind pointing at x20 and lets the later
backtrack from dl 16 clear the dl-15 entry.

Fix: equiv_lits holds only one equivalence per variable, so if the leading
variable already has one, handle the lineral as an ordinary unit. It is
still watched, so no propagation is lost.

Found by differential fuzzing (xnf_fuzzer.py) with a sanitizer build: it
shows with -il 5 (Gauss-elimination in-processing), e.g. with default
options plus -il 5 on a 799-variable 2-XNF instance. The release build gave
the right answer on it (UNSAT, as CryptoMiniSat), before and after the fix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/solver.hpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/solver.hpp b/src/solver.hpp
index cd342ec..ec3ac12 100644
--- a/src/solver.hpp
+++ b/src/solver.hpp
@@ -900,7 +900,9 @@ class solver
       }
 
       if(l.is_active(alpha)) {
-        if(opt.eq && l.is_equiv()) {
+        //an equiv found late, on a lower dl than the current one, may hit an LT that already has an equiv
+        //from a higher dl; equiv_lits holds only one per LT, so then treat l as a plain unit
+        if(opt.eq && l.is_equiv() && !equiv_lits[l.LT()].is_active()) {
           //if l is equiv!
           const var_t lt = l.LT();
           const var_t lt_other = l.get_equiv_lit();
-- 
2.55.0

